00:51:13.325 --> 00:51:19.261
To submit a DrivAerML result, open Run benchmarks and the DrivAerML quickstart.

673
00:51:20.002 --> 00:51:23.193
This local demo uses retained Transolver results.

674
00:51:25.053 --> 00:51:27.226
Fork and clone the submission repository.

675
00:51:27.967 --> 00:51:32.253
Create a branch from upstream main and install the pinned Linux environment.

676
00:51:32.993 --> 00:51:36.016
Keep the same checkout through evaluation and packaging.

677
00:51:37.861 --> 00:51:42.333
Run your surrogate first: the evaluator reads prediction arrays, not a model

678
00:51:42.333 --> 00:51:43.166
checkpoint.

679
00:51:43.906 --> 00:51:48.455
Each car needs surface pressure and three-component wall shear, plus volume pressure

680
00:51:48.455 --> 00:51:51.131
and velocity for surface-and-volume entries.

681
00:51:51.870 --> 00:51:56.432
Use finite, single or double precision arrays: one value per cell for

682
00:51:56.432 --> 00:51:58.244
pressure, three for vectors.

683
00:51:58.984 --> 00:52:03.520
Undo training normalization and retain native kinematic units for pressure and wall

684
00:52:03.520 --> 00:52:04.170
shear.

685
00:52:04.834 --> 00:52:08.141
Map outputs to every original cell in unchanged order.

686
00:52:08.881 --> 00:52:14.031
The supplied writer creates NPZ chunks, cell IDs and hashed manifests.

687
00:52:14.770 --> 00:52:17.252
Set the split and scope in the entry file.

688
00:52:19.109 --> 00:52:21.978
Scoring support makes comparisons consistent.

689
00:52:22.719 --> 00:52:26.812
Fetch data supplies the original mesh and published surface-area weights.

690
00:52:27.551 --> 00:52:32.899
Fetch support downloads verified CFD profile truth and sampling locations, pinned to

691
00:52:32.899 --> 00:52:33.732
the release.

692
00:52:34.471 --> 00:52:36.902
Everyone uses these same definitions.

693
00:52:37.641 --> 00:52:42.572
The evaluator integrates forces and extracts profiles from your predicted fields.

694
00:52:43.312 --> 00:52:47.977
Validate and evaluate the complete split with resume enabled: full uses fifty

695
00:52:47.977 --> 00:52:49.093
test cars.

696
00:52:49.832 --> 00:52:51.258
Inspect the report.

697
00:52:51.997 --> 00:52:57.397
Fields contribute fifty percent, forces twenty five percent, and fixed profiles twenty

698
00:52:57.397 --> 00:52:58.449
five percent.

699
00:52:59.188 --> 00:53:01.464
Relative profiles are report-only.

700
00:53:03.333 --> 00:53:07.839
Complete the method, compute, checkpoint and discretization records.

701
00:53:08.579 --> 00:53:12.351
Package and verify the result using your actual checkpoint files.

702
00:53:13.090 --> 00:53:16.693
Only the generated result directory goes into the pull request.

703
00:53:18.541 --> 00:53:21.165
Commit that directory and push to your fork.

704
00:53:21.906 --> 00:53:26.648
Compare across forks on GitHub: FluidsBench main is the base, your submission

705
00:53:26.648 --> 00:53:27.842
